M4+M5 (#959/#930): multi-input rendering + --watch

M4 (#959): `am render <a> <b> <c>` renders each file, emits
{ ok:true, files:[{index,file,ok,output|error}] }, skips bad files (like
#543). Single-input keeps the existing single-output behavior. Handles
the parseArgs boolean-flag quirk by collecting positionals (flags-last
convention; multi-positional is unambiguous).

M5 (#930): `am render <file> --watch` re-renders on fs.watch change.
Extracted renderFileOnce(file, format) as the pure, unit-testable
re-render step (svg/ascii/unicode/json); cmdRenderWatch wires it to
fs.watch + writes to --output or stdout. Live-watch timing isn't
unit-tested (fs.watch is nondeterministic in CI); the re-render core is
tested directly including a file-change-reflected case.

